I'm a Rogue (Chaotic, of course) with two magic lamps planning on
using them for my first wish. I was going to go GDSM, but then I got
to thinking... my AC is fine as is right now (-11 without any body
armor), what I really need is a MR source. Preferable one that won't
take up my robe slot, because, see, I've found all these neat
spellbooks (detect treasure, identify, cancellation, digging, and yes,
wizard lock to train on the matter spells) I could use help casting.
And while I'm at it, how about something that will help me regenerate
Power quickly?

So... that means I want the Eye of Aetc, right? But after remembering
a bad experience wishing for the PYEC and not being able to even pick
it up, I thought I'd read the spoiler. I did, and I *think* the
following portion is relelvant:

"If the artifact is intelligent, then in order to touch the artifact
safely, you must have the same alignment as the artifact, must be of
the same class (or no class is specified), must have non-negative
alignment, and must not be in the form of something the artifact
specially attacks. Otherwise, you will be blasted by the artifact's
power, sustain 4d10 damage (2d10 if you have magic-resistance), and
abuse your wisdom. If you are of the wrong class and have at least one
of the other conditions above, then the artifact will furthermore
"evade your grasp!" and you will not be able to use it at all."

So.... does this mean the Eye of Aetc is totally out of my reach?
